# A chatty task prints 100 times while two quiet ones print 3 each. The
# recording interleaves them A B C A B C A B C before the chatty one runs on,
# which is round-robin fairness — a property of the VM's deterministic scheduler
# profile, not a promise of `checkpoint()`, per the model owner's ruling of
# 2026-08-31.
#
# What the name of this row claims is still checked on native, and by the
# stronger half of the comparison. Measured on e34b7db8 at SURGE_THREADS=8, five
# runs: the order differed from the recording every time, and the set of lines
# was identical every time — B and C completed all three prints in every run,
# never later than the eleventh line. There is no starvation on native; there is
# no promised interleaving either. The multiset comparison is what says so, and
# it would fail if B or C were ever actually starved.
vm
